# Cursor repository rules

Read and follow `AGENTS.md` before changing code.

Run the quality gate after every change, before calling it complete: `python scripts/quality_check.py`. It runs five stages in a fixed order — build, unit tests and coverage, typecheck, lint, database schema — and reports all of them even when one fails. Build and coverage run first because lint findings mean nothing while the application does not import. While iterating, use `python scripts/quality_check.py --fast` to check only the files changed against the base branch and the working tree; it is a pre-check and does not run the aggregate or per-file coverage gate, so the full run is still required. Narrow to one stage with `--stage <name>`.

Every application change requires deterministic unit tests and the full coverage gate. Measure every `app/**/*.py` file without omissions and enforce >=90% statements, branches, and functions per file and in aggregate. Keep the global pytest timeout at 60 seconds. Mock external services (database, Redis, Celery, OpenAI, WhatsApp, Chroma, and network HTTP); mark live tests `integration` or `manual`. Never lower thresholds or add exclusions to hide untested application behavior. Include the complete coverage output in the completion report.

Lint and mypy are ratcheted against `quality-baseline.json`: fix new findings rather than raising a `max_findings` budget, and lower the budget in the same commit when a change improves a count. The `schema` stage validates `Base.metadata` offline; there is no Alembic in this repository, so `create_all` at boot is what applies pending tables, and it cannot alter an existing column.
